## 1. Executive framing

Pith is already defined consistently as a runtime-first, workspace-native orchestration system with governed autonomy, reusable traces, and Agent Company workflows layered on top of the core runtime.[1][2] The implementation gap is no longer product identity; it is execution fidelity: stable trace propagation, evaluation linkage, failure taxonomy adoption, cost attribution, and contract-level separation between Router, RuntimePlanner, ContextAssembler, Orchestrator, Memory, and governance surfaces.[5][2]

This epic converts the current aligned documentation into a concrete build sequence for v5.2.[4][3] The priority is not feature breadth; the priority is making the runtime explainable, replayable, governable, and economically attributable before autonomy or commercial workflows expand further.[1][2]

