## 3. Epic goals

### 3.1 Primary goals

- Stabilize the runtime around explicit contracts for Router, RuntimePlanner, ContextAssembler, Orchestrator, Memory, Evaluator, TaskService, ArtifactStore, and TraceStore.[4][2]
- Make every material execution path attributable by `trace_id`, `workspace_id`, `task_id`, `runtime_mode`, `runtime_config_version`, `failure_class`, and cost signals.[1][2]
- Connect evaluation and governance to production traces so regressions, unsafe autonomy, and expensive failure loops become measurable and reviewable.[6][2]
- Prepare the minimum substrate for Agent Company billing and department workflows without bypassing the core runtime.[1][3]

### 3.2 Non-goals

- No full multi-tenant SaaS platform in this epic.[4]
- No deep autonomous rollout beyond L0-L1 default operation; L2 remains gated by trace quality, evaluator maturity, and review controls.[1][2]
- No cosmetic dashboard overbuild before trace/event contracts are stable.[5][2]

